    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0489" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/715: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-12T11:00:00-05:00">January 12, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Leticia.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Brazilian Minister has presented Brazilian plan to Foreign Minister and
                        President and has so informed Rio de Janeiro. He states our note<anchor
                            n="23" xml:id="d391-f1"/> has made both Foreign Minister and President
                        furious.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>President and Foreign Minister refuse to accept second point in Brazilian
                        plan which is delivery of Leticia to Colombia stating Constituent Assembly
                        will not accept such a condition.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Manzanilla<anchor n="24" xml:id="d391-f2"/> informed Brazilian Minister
                        Peru desires Brazil to occupy Leticia holding it as a pledge until the
                        negotiations in Rio de Janeiro result in a final decision as to a new treaty
                        and the disposition of Leticia.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Brazilian Minister has telegraphed his Government expressing opinion Peru
                        merely wishes to neutralize Leticia by putting it in the hands of Brazil and
                        that Peru is unable to control the Peruvians in occupation there.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d391-f1" n="23" xml:id="d391-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 5, January 10, 5 p.m., to the Ambassador in Peru, <ref
                        target="#pg400">p. 400</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f2" n="24" xml:id="d391-f2-content">
                <p>J. M. Manzanilla, Peruvian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
